// `Shape.Circle(n)` constructs a `Shape`. The name before the dot is a declared
// type and the name after it is one of that type's payload-carrying variants, so
// there is no value to read off anything: the qualified name travels on the call
// and the answer is the type the source wrote before the dot. Lowering the callee
// as an expression asked for a binding of `Shape`, which no function binds, and
// reported E2001 for the load and E2004 for the member read after it.
//
// Reading the same name without calling it stays unanswered: a payload-carrying
// variant is a construction that needs its argument, and a constant would claim a
// value this pass cannot build. `tests/frontend/union_variant_read.orb` pins the
// payload-less sibling, which is a constant and answers.
import "../../compiler/tir/entry.orb"

fn main() {
    val source = "union Shape { Circle(int), Square }  fn make(n: int) -> Shape { return Shape.Circle(n) }"
    print(compileFrontendSource("fixture", source))
}
